.TH CREAT 3 "May 8, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
creat \- create a new file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <fcntl.h>
.PP
creat(name, mode)
    const char *name;
    int mode;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBThis interface is made obsolete by:\fP open(2).
.PP
.BR creat ()
is the same as:
.nf

    open(name, O_CREAT | O_TRUNC | O_WRONLY, mode);
.fi 
.SH "SEE ALSO"
open(2)
.SH "HISTORY"
The \fBcreat\fP function call appeared in Version 6 AT&T UNIX.
